.env
.secrets/*
!.secrets/*.pub
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
tubeworm/
.claude/worktrees/

# The Orca runtime's working directory. egress.py defaults its ledger to
# .orca/egress.jsonl (mode 0600) and the dispatch key lives here, so an unignored
# .orca/ lets a worker commit runtime state — and a private key — by accident (#300).
#
# `.orca/*`, not `.orca/`: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the
# negation below would not work under one. The public key is the exception on
# purpose — committing it is what turns dispatch-signature enforcement on
# (dispatch-sign.py:127), and an existing test says so.
.orca/*
!.orca/dispatch-pubkey

# Generated by scripts/bundle.py — a release artifact, never committed (21 copies of the
# doctrine tree would rot between runtime edits).
dist/
